# Binaries must never be line-ending-normalized on checkout. Without this a
# Windows client with core.autocrlf=true can corrupt a DLL, which then fails to
# load with HRESULT 0x80131515 - looking exactly like a zone block.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.nupkg binary
*.png binary
# Scripts keep CRLF on Windows; the UTF-8 BOM requirement is enforced by tests.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.md   text
*.json text
